== Trivia ==
* The achievement for unlocking Tainted Judas, "The Deceiver", may be reference to Judas Iscariot, the disciple who betrayed Jesus Christ, it may also be a reference to the Judas Priest song "Deceiver".
** This is also one of the meanings of his card, {{P|I - The Magician?}}, associated with manipulation and trickery.
* The assassin-type design of Tainted Judas, together with the {{i|Dark Arts}} he holds, might be inspired by a (not widely accepted) theory considering that the biblical Judas Iscariot belongs to the ''[[wikipedia:Sicarii|Sicarii]]'', a group of Jewish cloak-and-dagger assassins who strongly opposed the Roman occupation of Judea.
** The Sicarii, named after the word "Sicarius" which means dagger-wielder, are regarded as one of the earliest known organized assassination units of cloak and daggers. Sicarii were known to attack Romans and Roman sympathizers alike with daggers hidden in their cloak, then blending into the crowd after the deed to escape detection. The playstyle of Tainted Judas bears strong resemblance to this, while the sprite of {{i|Dark Arts}} can be a further evidence.
* Tainted Judas uses a modified version of {{C|Black Judas}}'s sprites, with the only difference being an additional costume that consists solely of the red cross brand and fez.
* Like all characters that start with only soul/black hearts, Tainted Judas' starting health is listed as "-I" on the character selection screen.
* {{i|Dark Arts}} is Black Judas' starting item in ''The Binding of Isaac: Four Souls''. Tainted Judas instead starts with Ceremonial Blade.
* The description of the unlockable {{P|Soul of Judas}} may be a reference to ''[https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=OR4N5OhcY9s Meet the Spy]'', in which the spy says, "Right behind you".

